attributes.description:
Makes the chip a toggle (a filter chip): its button gets `aria-pressed` from `selected`. A
`wc-chip-set` with `selectable` or `multiple` sets it on its chips and handles the selection;
a standalone selectable chip does not toggle itself, so the page sets `selected` on `click`.

example:
```html
<wc-code-highlighter language="javascript" label="hello.js" line-numbers highlight-lines="2"><pre><code>
  function helloWorld() {
    console.log('Hello, world!');
  }</code></pre>
</wc-code-highlighter>
```

attributes.description:
Where the menu opens relative to the button: `top`, `bottom`, `start` or `end`, optionally
followed by `-start` or `-end` (ADR-030001). `start` and `end` follow the writing direction;
the physical `left` / `right` still work but are deprecated. Defaults to `"bottom-start"`.

example:
```html
<wc-flow id="my-flow"></wc-flow>
<script>
  const flow = document.getElementById('my-flow');
  flow.nodes = [
    { id: '1', position: { x: 50, y: 50 }, data: { label: 'Node 1' } },
    { id: '2', position: { x: 250, y: 50 }, data: { label: 'Node 2' } }
  ];
  flow.edges = [
    { id: 'e1-2', source: '1', target: '2' }
  ];
</script>
```

```html
<wc-notification-manager placement="bottom-end"></wc-notification-manager>
<script>
  window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('peacock-toast', {
    detail: { title: 'Record saved', intent: 'success', dismissible: true }
  }));
</script>
```

attributes.description:
Preferred placement of the panel relative to the trigger: `top`, `bottom`, `start` or `end`,
optionally with `-start` or `-end` alignment. `start` and `end` follow the writing direction;
the physical `left` and `right` still work but are deprecated.

example:
```html
<style>
.ripple-surface {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 220px;
  height: 64px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  background: var(--color-surface-container-high);
  color: var(--color-on-surface);
  overflow: hidden;
  cursor: pointer;
  user-select: none;
}
</style>
<div class="ripple-surface">
  <wc-ripple></wc-ripple>
  Ripple Effect
</div>
```

